{#
	This block is deliberately NOT part of the metadata comment above (#452).

	The manifest fingerprint drops a leading comment that carries a `name:`
	line, because `usage:` and `category:` are per-project and regenerated
	downstream (#227). A fixture's Run: and Expected: lines are the opposite —
	skeleton-owned, and the only thing carrying the fixture's claim to truth.
	Kept inside that block, an upstream rewrite is invisible to drift
	detection: downstream keeps the old wording, verify reports OK, and
	fixtures.spec.js then fails on a fixture it cannot parse.
	Measured on eprukaz, 2026-07-30.
#}
{#
ComponentMetadataRule fixture — OK case.

Component template with a well-formed metadata block. Tests that:
- name is present and non-empty (required for all templates).
- category is present and non-empty (required for component templates).
- description is present but empty — allowed (description is optional, value may be "").
- All three optional URL/path keys are valid (asana on asana.com domain,
drupal as a site-relative path starting with '/', web as an absolute https URL).

Note: description is OPTIONAL — omitting it entirely is also valid and must NOT trigger
a warning. See component-metadata-fail-fixture.twig which omits description to verify no
spurious warning fires.

Page templates (those under templates/page/) are exempt from the category requirement.
The page-template exemption is exercised by the real page templates under
static/templates/page/ (e.g. article-full.twig, page-full.twig) which omit category
without triggering a warning. See component-metadata-page-ok-fixture.twig for the
documented example.

Run: vendor/bin/twig-cs-fixer lint --config tests/config/twig-wordpress.php tests/Fixtures/Twig/component-metadata-ok-fixture.twig
Expected: 0 warnings, 0 errors (ComponentMetadata)

The `fields:` block below carries a NESTED key named `category` (and `name`)
documenting the component's data shape. These must NOT shadow the top-level
`category: "Test"` / `name:` metadata — the parser only reads column-0 keys.
Regression guard for the nested-key shadowing bug.

fields:
		title: Name
		type: text
		title: Category
		type: group
		fields:
			title:
				title: Category title
				type: text
#}
{% extends '@component/component/component.twig' %}
